<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- UMW_Melee. Color. The grip and fittings are made of dark eltex: the accent half of the eltex
       pair, mirroring Anomaly's bioferrite stuff (sensitivity factor plus neural heat limit) where
       UMW_EltexPlated mirrors the eltex garments. Named for the fittings the accent mask actually
       paints, in the zeus-headed / plasma-cored furniture register (chosen over eltex-threaded,
       -veined and -filigreed). INTENT: "a weapon whose furniture amplifies a psycaster."
       Routing: Core's PsychicSensitivity carries StatPart_GearStatFactor and PsychicEntropyMax a
       StatPart_GearStatOffset, both with includeWeapon, reading the primary weapon's
       PsychicSensitivityFactor / PsychicEntropyMaxOffset as weapon-thing stats; CompUniqueWeapon's
       GetStatFactor / GetStatOffset hand them this trait's statFactors / statOffsets and the pawn's
       breakdown lists the weapon under "Relevant gear" (the heat-limit OFFSET line needs
       Patches/StatPart_GearStatOffset_WeaponRelevantGear_Patch.cs to open vanilla's gate; the factor
       line never did). No hediff, no TraitEffectSummary case. Neither stat has a quality part, so
       both values are flat across qualities (the warcasket pair included).
       Anchors: bioferrite's normal-quality pair (x1.10, +8), with the heat limit rounded up to +10;
       MarketValue +100, a step under Plated's +120 (added capability is an offset). On a weapon that
       also rolls Plated the factor multiplies the summed offsets (vanilla's gear stacking), the
       intended full-set reward, still under the eltex staff (Plated's header has the ceiling).
       Double-edged by construction: amplified sensitivity raises exposure to psychic drones and
       lances, which is why the pair carries no malus.
       Tokens: Color only. It forces UMW_EltexShade onto colour one via vanilla forcedColor, so it is
       an alternative to the Gold/Jade inlays, Envenomed and ZeusHeaded, and to UMW_LeadLined, which
       also carries Color. It deliberately does NOT carry Eltex: it must co-roll with Plated (body
       channel), and Color already excludes it from the lining.
       Root: eltex is Royalty canon and every vanilla eltex item is techLevel Ultra, so the def lives
       in the Royalty compat root (the folder is the gate, no MayRequire) and the war merchant's
       scoped ultratech ban in Patches/CompUniqueWeapon_DisabledTraits_Patch.cs names it. VPE's
       medieval eltex weapons are not followed. canGenerateAlone true, a real effect; commonality
       0.35, Plated's, rather than the trio's 0.5: two eltex traits at 0.5 would roughly double eltex
       presence against Monomolecular, PlasmaCored and ZeusHeaded. -->
  <WeaponTraitDef>
    <defName>UMW_EltexFitted</defName>
    <label>eltex-fitted</label>
    <description>The grip and fittings are made of dark, unpolished eltex. They enhance the wielder's psychic sensitivity and increase their neural heat limit.</description>
    <commonality>0.35</commonality>
    <weaponCategory>UMW_Melee</weaponCategory>
    <exclusionTags>
      <li>Color</li>
    </exclusionTags>
    <forcedColor>UMW_EltexShade</forcedColor>
    <statOffsets>
      <PsychicEntropyMaxOffset>10</PsychicEntropyMaxOffset> <!-- not quality-scaled; bioferrite normal is +8 -->
      <MarketValue>100</MarketValue> <!-- a step under Plated's +120 -->
    </statOffsets>
    <statFactors>
      <PsychicSensitivityFactor>1.1</PsychicSensitivityFactor> <!-- not quality-scaled; bioferrite normal is x1.10 -->
    </statFactors>
    <traitAdjectives>
      <li>eltex-fitted</li>
      <li>eltex-furnished</li>
      <li>resonant</li>
    </traitAdjectives>
  </WeaponTraitDef>

</Defs>
